    <!--
      V9 — Redesigned to match the supplied JSX visual reference
      (minimalist dark controller, thin outlines, edge-anchored control
      groups, large clear center gameplay area) while keeping every id,
      view class, and GamepadActivity wiring from V8 unchanged.

      All 19 control positions were generated + collision/clipping
      checked programmatically (circle-vs-circle distance test, min 14px
      gap, against a 1536x768 = 2:1 landscape reference) rather than
      hand-measured — see the accompanying layout_calc.py used to derive
      these bias values. No two controls overlap and nothing clips a
      screen edge at these values.

      Formula used (1:1 square view, height_percent P, on a 2:1 W=2H screen):
        width_px = height_px = P * H
        H_bias = (cx_px - P*H/2) / (W - P*H)
        V_bias = (cy_px - P*H/2) / (H - P*H)

      SIZES (as height_percent):
        Shoulder (LT/LB/RB/RT):        0.1302  — now circular, same size
                                                  as D-pad/ABXY (JSX uses a
                                                  uniform circular size for
                                                  all of these, not a larger
                                                  distinct shoulder shape)
        D-pad / ABXY buttons:           0.1302  — unified size (JSX draws
                                                  these the same size)
        L3 / R3:                        0.1250
        Home:                           0.1250
        View / Menu:                    0.1016
        JoystickView:                   0.2995  — enlarged from V8's 0.28
                                                  to better fill the screen
                                                  per the "use the whole
                                                  landscape screen" brief

      CENTERS (x%, y% of screen):
        LT (5.2,15.5)  LB (14.8,15.5)  RB (85.2,15.5)  RT (94.8,15.5)
        View(38.3,8.5) Home(46.0,9.0)  Menu(53.5,8.5)
        DUp(9.5,31.0) DLeft(3.5,41.4) DRight(15.5,41.4) DDown(9.5,51.8)
        Y(90.5,31.0)  X(84.5,41.4)   B(96.5,41.4)      A(90.5,51.8)
        LJS(12.0,75.0)  RJS(88.0,75.0)
        L3(4.0,93.0)    R3(96.0,93.0)

      V10 — SPACING-ONLY PASS (no visual/design/size changes; every id,
      view class, drawable, color, and size_percent above is untouched).
      Only leftJoystick / rightJoystick bias values moved:
        - Every other control (shoulders, D-pad, ABXY, View/Home/Menu,
          L3/R3) already sits within ~0.2%–2% of its nearest screen edge
          or neighbor, so there was no meaningful slack left to reclaim
          there without touching size or introducing overlap risk.
        - The joysticks were the one group with real unused margin
          (8% empty horizontal margin vs. ~0.2%-2% for every other
          edge-hugging control, plus a near-zero 0.215%-of-height gap
          to the D-pad/ABXY row above them). They were pulled outward
          toward the side edges (15.5%→12.0% / 84.5%→88.0% x) and
          nudged down (73.5%→75.0% y), which simultaneously:
            1) closes most of that unused side margin,
            2) opens the D-pad/ABXY→joystick vertical gap from 0.215%
               to ~1.7% of screen height (was uncomfortably tight),
            3) still leaves 21.9px clearance to L3/R3 and 17.3px
               clearance to the D-pad (both > the 14px min-gap rule
               used throughout this layout), and
            4) leaves the joystick bottom edge at 89.975% — well clear
               of the screen bottom, so L3/R3 are not pushed off-screen.
        - Net effect: the open central gameplay gap between the two
          joysticks actually grows (from ~54% to ~61% of screen width),
          satisfying "keep the central gameplay area clear" while still
          reducing the dead margin on the left/right edges.

      V11 — EDGE-SAFETY PASS. Note on ConstraintLayout bias semantics:
      every control here is anchored with BOTH Start_toStartOf="parent"
      AND End_toEndOf="parent" (same for Top/Bottom). With that dual-
      anchor pattern, `bias` is the view's position as a fraction of the
      *remaining free space* (parentSize − viewSize), not a fraction of
      the raw parent size — so centerX = bias·(W−size) + size/2. That
      guarantees left = bias·(W−size) ≥ 0 and right ≤ W for any bias in
      [0,1]: the full view rectangle can never leave the parent in this
      setup, regardless of how close to 0/1 the bias looks. Full-rect
      audit (left/right/top/bottom vs parent, not just center) confirmed
      zero clipping in V10.
      That said, a few edge margins were uncomfortably thin for real
      touch/gesture-zone safety (btnDpadLeft & btnB: 3.7px; L3/R3
      bottom: 5.8px) versus this file's own 14px minimum-gap standard
      used everywhere else. Fixed by translating whole shapes (not
      resizing/re-deriving them) so geometry is preserved exactly:
        - D-pad cross shifted +10.3px right (all 4 buttons, same delta)
        - ABXY diamond shifted −10.3px left (all 4 buttons, same delta)
        - L3 and R3 both nudged +8.2px up (independently, still mirrored)
      All edge margins are now ≥13.4px and all neighbor-to-neighbor
      clearances (D-pad↔joystick, joystick↔L3/R3, ABXY↔joystick, etc.)
      are ≥15.4px — at or above the 14px standard already used
      throughout this file. No sizes, colors, ids, view classes, or
      Kotlin were touched.

      V12 — COMPOSITION PASS, targeting the Far Cry 5 HUD reference.
      Sizes, colors, drawables, view classes, ids, and touch handling
      are all UNCHANGED — RoundButtonView/ShoulderButtonView/JoystickView
      onDraw already closely matches the reference's language (thin
      single-stroke outline, transparent interior, dotted-texture stick
      cap), so this pass is positioning only.
        - Reworked the previous edge-hugging margins (13-14px, from the
          V11 clipping-safety pass) into genuinely comfortable ones
          (~35-225px) per this brief's explicit "do not push controls
          against the physical edge" direction — a deliberate reversal
          of V9-V11's "push to edge" instructions, since this turn's
          brief supersedes them.
        - LT, the D-pad's left edge, and L3 are now aligned to the SAME
          x-column (a straight vertical line down the left side), matching
          the reference's left-hand control column. RT/ABXY-right-edge/R3
          mirror this on the right.
        - D-pad and ABXY were each translated as a single rigid unit
          (same internal cross/diamond geometry, only repositioned) so
          "D-pad remains a proper cross" / "ABXY remains a proper
          diamond" hold automatically - verified centers mirror to
          0.1px.
        - leftJoystick/rightJoystick moved in from the edge (12%→12.4%
          of remaining space, i.e. ~18% of screen width) to sit more
          centrally under their cluster rather than edge-anchored,
          matching the reference's proportionally larger, more central
          stick placement, while keeping the same view size.
        - L3/R3 moved up ~21px to sit closer to/more associated with
          their stick (per reference), while keeping ≥21.9px clearance
          to the stick and ≥35px from the bottom edge.
        - Re-validated the full 19-control set directly from the saved
          XML: zero clipping, zero overlaps, minimum gap 21.9px (up
          from V11's 14-15px), central gameplay gap between the two
          sticks still ~55% of screen width.

      V13 — STICK-ONLY INWARD PASS. Only leftJoystick/rightJoystick
      Horizontal_bias touched (12.37%→28.83% and 87.63%→71.17% of
      remaining space); vertical bias, size, and every other control
      are byte-for-byte unchanged.
        - leftJoystick center moves from ~18.0% to ~32.0% of screen
          width; rightJoystick mirrors it at ~68.0%. Both sticks were
          directly beside the D-pad/ABXY column, so moving them toward
          center only increases (never decreases) their clearance to
          the D-pad, ABXY, and L3/R3 — verified via the same
          circle-vs-circle distance check used in V9-V12: min gap
          actually grows from ~18-22px to ~210px+.
        - Central gameplay gap between the two stick's inner edges is
          now ~323px (~21% of screen width) — still an open center
          area, just no longer 55%+ of the screen.

      V14 — VERTICAL-ONLY PASS. Only Vertical_bias touched on 12
      controls; every Horizontal_bias, size, id, and every other
      control (joysticks, L3/R3, View/Home/Menu, status bar) is
      byte-for-byte unchanged.
        - btnLT/btnLB/btnRB/btnRT: 0.1034→0.0765 (all four moved up
          by the same ~18px delta, so the shoulder row stays level
          and symmetrical left/right).
        - btnDpadUp/Left/Right/Down: 0.2816/0.401/0.401/0.5207 →
          0.3086/0.428/0.428/0.5476 (all four rows shifted down by
          the same ~18px delta — the cross's internal spacing is
          identical, only translated).
        - btnY/X/B/A: 0.2816/0.401/0.401/0.5207 →
          0.3086/0.428/0.428/0.5476 (same ~18px down delta as the
          D-pad, so the diamond's internal spacing is unchanged and
          D-pad/ABXY move down together in lockstep).
        - Re-checked clearance after the shift: shoulders moving up
          only increases their gap to the View/Home/Menu row above
          and to the D-pad/ABXY below (both already far apart), and
          D-pad/ABXY moving down toward the (untouched) joysticks
          still leaves ~150px of circle-to-circle clearance — no new
          clipping or overlap introduced.
    -->

